../design.md:1:# Experiment design: Topic When that package is independently executed in the locked environment, do the regenerated CSV files reproduce the three stated SHA-256 digests exactly? _(auto-enqueued follow-up from topic-can-a-raw-per-seed-file-be-released-contai)_
../design.md:3:**Hypothesis:** Across four executions in fresh locked environments with the output directory initially absent, syscall tracing will show that each of the three target CSV paths is created after execution begins, is written before any read of that path, and produces its assigned stated SHA-256 digest in every run.
../design.md:6:Execute the supplied package four times in newly created, network-isolated Linux containers and require syscall-level creation/write-before-read provenance plus exact stated SHA-256 reproduction for all three CSV targets in all 12 run-target combinations.
../design.md:9:1. At the workspace root, create experiment_manifest.json before any package execution. It must contain: schema_version equal to 1; experiment_id; container_image as an immutable Linux ARM64 image reference including an @sha256 digest and containing Python 3 and strace; platform equal to linux/arm64; package_inputs as a nonempty array of objects with host_path, container_path under /inputs, and lowercase 64-hex sha256; optional setup_argv as an array of argument arrays for offline installation or setup; execution_argv as a nonempty argument array containing the literal placeholder {output_dir}; working_directory as an absolute container path; timeout_seconds between 1 and 300; and target_csvs as exactly three objects, each having a unique id, a safe relative_path ending in .csv, and a lowercase 64-hex stated_sha256 copied from the package's published declaration rather than calculated from experimental output. Reject absolute target paths, .. path components, duplicate paths or IDs, floating image tags, shell command strings, and unknown manifest fields.
../design.md:10:2. Implement a JSON Schema for this structure and a semantic validator. Before execution, validate the manifest; verify every package input exists, is a regular file, and matches its declared SHA-256; verify the three stated digests and their documentary source are available; verify execution_argv resolves to an executable package entry point; and verify no target path can escape {output_dir}. Save manifest_validation.json with pass/fail details. Any failure is a preflight abort and must not produce hypothesis-level success or failure rates.
../design.md:11:3. Select Docker or Podman. Require a functioning Linux engine by running its information command and a no-network test container from the exact locally available manifest image. Do not pull an image during the experiment. Confirm that the image architecture is linux/arm64, that strace and Python 3 execute, and that ptrace works by tracing a one-line Python process. Docker may use --cap-add=SYS_PTRACE --security-opt=seccomp=unconfined; use equivalent Podman settings. If Podman is selected on macOS, initialize and start its machine before this preflight. Record engine name, version, image ID/digest, architecture, and ptrace-test result in preflight.json. Abort without rates if any check fails.
../design.md:12:4. Test the trace parser before package runs. Use strace with -f -ttt -T -yy -s 4096 and a single ordered log file. The parser must handle successful execve, open/openat/openat2/creat, close, dup/dup2/dup3, chdir/fchdir, read/pread64/readv/preadv, write/pwrite64/writev/pwritev, truncate/ftruncate, mmap with readable or writable file mappings, rename/renameat/renameat2, link, unlink, fork/vfork/clone, failed calls, and unfinished/resumed calls. Normalize paths lexically and by fd annotations emitted by -yy. Count only successful syscalls. A target creation event is a successful open-family call with O_CREAT that returns an fd annotated with the normalized target path; creation solely by renaming or linking a temporary file does not satisfy the stated direct-write hypothesis. A target read or write event is the first successful positive-byte read-family or write-family operation on an fd annotated with that target; a readable mmap is a read and a writable mmap is a write. Zero-byte operations do not count.
../design.md:13:5. Run automated parser controls: a handcrafted passing trace with create, positive-byte write, close, reopen, and read; a failing trace with create-read-write ordering; a failing trace lacking creation; a failing atomic-rename trace; traces containing child PIDs and unfinished/resumed calls; and a digest-mismatch fixture. Also run two live traced controls in the selected image: control_good.py must start with an absent CSV, create it using O_CREAT, write fixed bytes, close it, then read it and be classified as passing; control_bad.py must start with an absent CSV, create it read-only, attempt a one-byte read, then reopen and write it and be classified as read-before-write. Require every expected classification and require the good control's computed digest to equal an independently hard-coded fixture digest. Save parser_control_results.json. Abort without package executions or hypothesis-level rates if any control fails.
../design.md:14:6. Create four host run roots named runs/run_01 through runs/run_04. Immediately before each run, delete and recreate only the run root, leaving runs/run_N/output absent. Confirm with lstat that output and all three target paths are absent. Never seed, copy, cache, or restore files into the output path. Store this absence check and its timestamp in run_N/precheck.json.
../design.md:15:7. For each run, create a new container with --rm, --network=none, --read-only, --pull=never, --pids-limit=256, a 4 GB memory limit, and at most 4 CPUs. Mount every package input read-only at its manifest container_path, mount the run root read-write at /runs/current, and use tmpfs mounts for /tmp and /venv. Do not mount prior run directories, user home directories, package caches, or the workspace. Set HOME=/tmp/home, PYTHONHASHSEED=0, TZ=UTC, LC_ALL=C.UTF-8, and SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=1704067200. Use no randomness; if the package accepts a seed, pass seed 1729 in execution_argv and keep it identical across runs.
../design.md:17:9. Replace {output_dir} in execution_argv with /runs/current/output and start the package under strace: strace -f -ttt -T -yy -s 4096 -o /runs/current/trace.log followed by the direct execution argv. The first successful execve of execution_argv is the execution-begin event. Enforce the manifest timeout, record exit status and elapsed time, and retain stdout.txt and stderr.txt. Do not retry or repair a failed run; a timeout, nonzero exit, missing trace, or unparseable trace is a measured run failure.
../design.md:18:10. After each container exits, require each target to exist at runs/run_N/output/<relative_path>, be a regular file rather than a symlink, and remain within the output directory after realpath resolution. Compute SHA-256 by streaming raw bytes with Python hashlib.sha256 using 1 MiB chunks. Do not normalize line endings, parse CSV content, or modify files before hashing.
../design.md:19:11. Parse trace.log in its recorded line order. For each target, require: the pre-container and pre-execution absence checks passed; a successful creation event occurred after the execution-begin execve; at least one positive-byte direct write occurred after creation; no positive-byte read or readable mmap of that target occurred before its first write; and the final digest equals stated_sha256. Record event line numbers, timestamps, PIDs, syscall names, resolved paths, byte counts, actual digest, expected digest, and individual Boolean checks in run_N/results.json. If a target is created via rename/link, only memory-mapped without a writable mapping, or cannot be resolved unambiguously, mark its provenance check failed rather than guessing.
../design.md:20:12. Require exactly four attempted package executions and exactly 12 run-target result records. Use the stated digest as the comparison baseline and each run's raw-file digest as the measured value; use the parser's deliberately bad control as the ordering-negative baseline. No denominator may exclude failed, missing, timed-out, or malformed run-target records. If preflight succeeded but fewer than 12 records are recoverable, classify the completed experiment as refuted due to incomplete required observations while reporting the missing-count explicitly.
../design.md:21:13. Produce aggregate_results.json and aggregate_results.csv with one row per run-target pair. Compute the metrics below. The hypothesis is supported only if all preflights and controls passed, four executions occurred, 12 records exist, and every required rate is exactly 1.0. With complete preflight, any package-run failure, missing observation, digest mismatch, absent/late creation, missing write, or read-before-write event refutes the hypothesis.
../design.md:22:14. Generate result_matrix.png using matplotlib. Draw a 4-by-3 heatmap with runs as rows and target IDs as columns. Encode green only when creation, write-before-read, and digest checks all pass; red otherwise. Annotate each cell with C, O, and D as 1 or 0 for creation, ordering, and digest, plus the first eight hexadecimal characters of the actual digest or MISSING. Include a title stating the number of fully passing combinations out of 12 and save at 1600 by 900 pixels or larger.
../design.md:23:15. Finish within 30 minutes. Suggested limits are 3 minutes for validation and controls, 5 minutes maximum per package execution, and 5 minutes for parsing, hashing, aggregation, and plotting. Distinguish preflight-aborted from supported or refuted: a missing manifest, engine, image, trace capability, or package input yields only a preflight-aborted result and no hypothesis-level rates.
../design.md:26:- execution completeness = number of package executions attempted divided by 4; the required value is 1.0
../design.md:30:- digest reproduction rate = records whose raw-byte SHA-256 equals the assigned stated SHA-256 divided by 12; the required value is 1.0
../design.md:31:- joint pass rate = records simultaneously passing absence, creation, write-before-read, file-safety, and digest checks divided by 12; support requires exactly 12/12 = 1.0
../design.md:32:- per-target reproducibility = for each of the three targets, matching digests across all four runs divided by 4; each target must equal 4/4 = 1.0
../design.md:39:- **If supported:** All preflight and parser controls pass; exactly 4 fresh-container package executions and 12 run-target observations are recorded; every target is absent before its run, directly created after execution begins, positively written before any positive-byte read, and hashes to its assigned stated SHA-256 in all four runs. Creation-after-start, write-before-read, digest reproduction, per-target reproducibility, and joint pass rates are all exactly 1.0, and all 12 heatmap cells are green with C=1, O=1, and D=1.
../design.md:40:- **If refuted:** After successful preflight, any of the following refutes the hypothesis: fewer than 4 successful required executions or fewer than 12 observations, any target existing before execution, no qualifying post-start direct creation, a read or readable mmap before the first positive-byte write, no positive-byte write, unsafe/missing output, or any final SHA-256 differing from its stated digest. At least one required rate will be below 1.0 and at least one heatmap cell will be red. If prerequisites or parser controls fail, the result is preflight-aborted rather than evidence for or against the hypothesis, and no hypothesis-level rates are emitted.
